65622143001-f35a1d10-1d9c-46f0-8bfe-1971ec1b53b5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d3a6b4e3eae9f6aa6b2573500e3000c4509e39bc1dcd729021c184fdbc2a616f","event_uuid":"d87f1b26-f9c8-49b5-9b9d-1bbb771c9bcd","position":{"commit_sha":"3b458e21be0fbb84562f19e2add52638dffbb1e2","position":"1786746930334561001-d87f1b26-f9c8-49b5-9b9d-1bbb771c9bcd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a84040fe8815c5074d27a12aba10751d3b6543661f1633322fad8492e3e9c6da","event_uuid":"5d4c56ad-fb23-4b1d-abfe-9a0443bf049d","position":{"commit_sha":"df723bfaed85d7568a40b1f2ba8fe438116d399d","position":"1786747572943943001-5d4c56ad-fb23-4b1d-abfe-9a0443bf049d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OSS / BUILD-VS-REUSE CHECK (2026-08-14; pinned main SHAs)\n\nSurveyed popular active test-heavy projects: pytest-dev/pytest (14.4k stars, 68308aa), pypa/pip (10.2k, f399c371), python-poetry/poetry (92b74dc), and pre-commit/pre-commit (15.5k, 9767b6c). All four isolate mutable state into pytester/tmp_path/temp Git repos or mock Git and none runs source-checkout `git rev-parse HEAD` before and after every test. pip has an autouse isolate fixture that remaps HOME/config into tmpdir; Poetry uses autouse tmp working directories and a Git mock; pre-commit creates all mutable Git repos under temp fixtures; pytest uses pytester/temp paths and only lightweight autouse environment resets. This is 4/4 consensus for keeping source-checkout VCS subprocesses out of the per-test hot path, with no documented rejection.\n\nHowever, the implementation primitive does NOT have consensus. Poetry uses Dulwich Repo for in-process Git semantics; pip and pre-commit deliberately use Git CLI/rev-parse in their Git-facing code (1/3 library, 2/3 CLI). None of the four maintains the stricter per-test checkout-HEAD attribution guard rebar requires. Removing that guard would match their baseline but violates this ticket/session fidelity constraint. Adding Dulwich/pygit2/GitPython solely for two metadata reads is not supported by 2/3 consensus and adds install/import/dependency surface to every test job. Hand-parsing symbolic/loose/packed/worktree refs is likewise not an OSS-consensus practice and carries the plan-review advisory around pack-refs/reftable correctness.\n\nDecision under the standing rule: the direction (eliminate 26k-ish per-suite source Git process launches) is consensus-backed, but neither fidelity-preserving implementation option reaches the automatic-approval bar. No production/test code changed. Retain the measured candidate (~75s projected macOS wall saving; ~207 runner-s) for operator disposition while higher-confidence editor and mutation RCA work continues.","timestamp":1786747572943943001}],"created_at":1786746680504403001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"43253c46-803e-4ca7-8f42-a30410f83268","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4f50-b1f2-78af-4326"}],"description":"## Context\nThe default suite runs about 13,255 tests. The autouse _no_repo_commits guard calls git rev-parse HEAD before and after every test. On macOS, 1,000 direct head() probes averaged 7.826ms, projecting 207.4 runner-seconds / 69.1 three-worker wall-seconds per full job. A same-host A-B-B-A experiment over 895 tests measured baseline 51.81s and 56.70s versus 49.22s and 49.21s when only this guard was bypassed: median saving 5.04s (9.3%), projecting about 75s at full-suite scale. The session-wide dirty-tree backstop remains separate. No matching performance ticket was found; closed renderer ticket ashy-waterlog-hamadryas mentions the guard only as failure attribution, not optimization.\n\n## Plan\n- Preserve the exact per-test contract: detect a checkout HEAD move, name the responsible test, retain the current allow_repo_writes escape, and retain the session dirty-tree backstop.\n- Replace two per-test Git processes with an in-process HEAD fingerprint after one-time per-worker discovery of the worktree Git directory/common directory. Cover symbolic loose refs, packed refs, detached HEAD, and linked worktrees; fall back safely when metadata is unreadable.\n- Inventory callers and string-based references before changing the shared primitive.\n- Write RED behavioral tests for unchanged HEAD, same-branch commit, detached commit, packed-ref-to-loose transition, linked-worktree commit, and exact test attribution. Add a subprocess spy proving steady-state per-test checks launch no Git process.\n- Compare the approach with test-isolation/checkout-integrity practice in at least three popular actively maintained OSS projects. Implement only if at least two-thirds use the practice and none documents rejecting it for coverage/reliability; otherwise return the research for operator disposition.\n- Repeat the 895-test A-B-B-A experiment and report full-suite projected plus observed savings without weakening any test selection or assertion.\n- Land through Gerrit; back out with a Gerrit revert if any supported Git layout regresses or CI savings fail to reproduce.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Same-branch, detached-HEAD, packed-ref, and linked-worktree HEAD moves are detected by behavioral tests.\n- [ ] An unchanged HEAD produces no false positive.\n- [ ] The failing test remains individually named and allow_repo_writes retains its existing behavior.\n- [ ] Steady-state before/after checks execute no Git subprocess per test after one-time worker initialization.\n- [ ] The session dirty-tree backstop and all existing repo-isolation tests remain enabled.\n- [ ] Three named active OSS projects are compared and the consensus decision is recorded against the standing approval rule.\n- [ ] Paired timing shows a positive median wall-time reduction on the same 895-test slice and reports the full-suite projection.\n- [ ] Focused tests, full lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 are recorded before merge.\n- [ ] The first post-merge full-route macOS observation is recorded before close.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_isolation.py","reason":"Replace per-test Git subprocess HEAD probes with an in-process fingerprint that preserves supported Git layouts."},{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"Initialize and consume the optimized per-worker repo-head probe without weakening per-test attribution."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py","reason":"Prove same-branch, detached, packed-ref, linked-worktree, fallback, and no-subprocess behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d87f1b26-f9c8-49b5-9b9d-1bbb771c9bcd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","tests"],"ticket_id":"3bfb-e6c6-ba97-4a69","ticket_type":"task","title":"Eliminate per-test Git subprocesses from repo-isolation guard","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["63223ce9-a90c-4abd-958d-42c6c75d98b4","43253c46-803e-4ca7-8f42-a30410f83268","c0bde991-81e2-4ee1-a0d1-c4ecb38a24e1","f35a1d10-1d9c-46f0-8bfe-1971ec1b53b5","d87f1b26-f9c8-49b5-9b9d-1bbb771c9bcd","5d4c56ad-fb23-4b1d-abfe-9a0443bf049d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786750683212056001,"uuid":"90e6e183-7d93-45cb-aad4-ffe86a54ec02"}